Subject: [PATCH] 5347: a request passed on by a link travels for the owner
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Tester 61837: link A, asked to introduce the owner to T, said "I don't know
her, but B does — ask B in my name". A's assistant opened a request of A's
own, so B read "A's assistant asks you to introduce A to T" and the owner's
need became A's. There was no request that is passed on.

In A's own request thread, request_introduction now passes the owner's
request on: the requester stays the owner (with the owner's target, reason
and goal), B is found in A's phonebook, and the request records A in a new
column, introduction_requests.forwarded_by_user_id (migration 244). B's
opening line and push name whose assistant passed it on, for whom. The
owner's outgoing thread opens as for any request, so the owner sees it.

New person-facing text (B's opening in four languages and the push):
held until Misho's yes and Giorgi's OK of the exact words (D44, D582).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
